WEBVTT

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:24.820
<v Speaker 1>Hello, and welcome to the 2004 Magic the Gathering World Championships. I'm Randy Mueller. I'm the Director of Magic R&amp;D, and I'll be your host for these opening ceremonies. First of all, congratulations on getting here. 301 of you are competing representing 56 different countries, and I can still remember what it felt like to sit right where you are. People ask me all the time if I missed playing on the Pro Tour. Absolutely.</v>

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:40.670
<v Speaker 1>Every time I come to one of the events, I wish I could step into the arena just like you guys are, feel that adrenaline rush and compete again. Most of the time I like my job better, but I definitely encourage you to treasure this week and this weekend. These moments are special and your experiences this week will be well worth savoring, I trust.</v>

00:00:42.230 --> 00:01:11.120
<v Speaker 1>Next, I'd like to take this opportunity to let you all know how the game is doing in general. Sort of the state of the brand address. I'm delighted to say things are better than ever. Last year we celebrated Magic's 10 year anniversary. It turned out to be our biggest, our best year ever. Sanctioned tournament numbers are up, sales are up. We've extended the game onto an online platform now and in my opinion are designers keep coming up with an awesome new cards and mechanics. New generations of TCG players keep growing up and discovering what you guys already know. All roads lead to Magic.</v>

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:27.210
<v Speaker 1>This year we're celebrating the 10th anniversary of Worlds, and the game has gotten bigger still. One of you is gonna go down in history, get your name carved on that trophy back there. The rest of you are gonna have to settle for splitting up $1,000,000 in prize money and making us add more to the big display there.</v>

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:40.040
<v Speaker 1>At the end of the day though, Magic isn't really all about the money. At its core, Magics a kick ass strategy game. It's fun to think about, it's fun to talk about, and most importantly, it's just plain fun to play.</v>

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:49.730
<v Speaker 1>I actually considered a great honor to work on such a great game. I always tell people that my goal is to do my job well enough, that the Pro Tour will still be here for me when I retire.</v>

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:56.900
<v Speaker 1>So it's now my great privilege to introduce you to the man who's ultimately responsible for bringing us all here this week.</v>

00:01:57.690 --> 00:02:14.320
<v Speaker 1>14 years ago it was a math professor like to spend his free time playing games and tinkering around with their rules. He approached the fledgling game company called Wizards of the Coast in order to try to sell them a board game called Robo Rally. They formed a relationship that would eventually revolutionize the entire gaming industry</v>

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:23.000
<v Speaker 1>is continued tinkering. Sue led him to invent the whole new genre of games, and a couple of years later, Magic the Gathering was released and immediately became a smash hit.</v>

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:38.580
<v Speaker 1>After 11 years, hundreds of competitors, thousands of different cards and many millions of players, Magic is still the premier trading card game and we owe it all to this man. Ladies and gentlemen, Magic's original designer, Doctor Richard Garfield.</v>

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:46.220
<v Speaker 2>Hi.</v>

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:51.740
<v Speaker 2>Since the stakes are so high, I thought I'd take this opportunity to talk about politics.</v>

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:54.460
<v Speaker 2>I'm just kidding.</v>

00:02:55.770 --> 00:03:13.120
<v Speaker 2>See if I can get a rise out of the event coordinators. I'm really happy to be here. This event means a lot to me. I've attended almost every year. I would risk missing the birth of my child to be here, as I proved five years ago in Japan.</v>

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:18.960
<v Speaker 2>And I'm not alone in that sentiment. Randy running that risk right now.</v>

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:41.560
<v Speaker 2>I've used this analogy before to describe what it feels like for me, but I'll use it again. If I were a composer, this would be like the world's best musicians coming together to play my music. And, and I think there is some truth to that analogy, but I'm not a composer on the game designer</v>

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:47.450
<v Speaker 2>and I'm proud to be a game designer. Games are amazing things.</v>

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:55.290
<v Speaker 2>They are training for your mind in the same way that sports are training for your body.</v>

00:03:56.950 --> 00:03:58.910
<v Speaker 2>It's that belief which has led me to</v>

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:01.980
<v Speaker 2>convert my home into a mental gymnasium.</v>

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:05.310
<v Speaker 2>My family is in constant training.</v>

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:18.770
<v Speaker 2>I often hear the cries around my house. Daddy, play another game. Daddy, it's time for a game, or Daddy Skylar won't let me choose the next game.</v>

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:30.690
<v Speaker 2>You've heard of the Suzuki method for training children to play violin? Well, I'm using it to train gaming virtuosos, I hope.</v>

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:52.570
<v Speaker 2>Recently I've had my eyes set on Magic and I've had little decks constructed specifically for the little hand so that they can hold the properly. And the cries around the house have changed somewhat. Now I hear Daddy Skyler won't let me play her card because Skyler likes to play controlled X.</v>

00:04:54.860 --> 00:05:01.810
<v Speaker 2>And when I've taught them all I can, I'm going to send them off to train under Chi and under Finkel,</v>

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:13.380
<v Speaker 2>and then they'll be able to come here to world with me and see for themselves first hand what makes this event so special as they play against people from all over the world for days on end.</v>

00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:18.520
<v Speaker 2>So play hard, play fair, and have fun.</v>

